      "summary": "Spike: Contentful Integration Technical Design & Content Model",
      "description": "Objective\nReview and finalise the Contentful Integration Technical Design Document (TSD) produced under SFCC-123, ensuring it is accurate, complete, and ready to serve as the reference artefact for the incoming Contentful squad and the SFCC build team.\nBackground\nThe initial Contentful Integration TSD was drafted as part of SFCC-123, covering the Contentful → MRT → SFCC integration pattern, content model requirements, locale configuration, and SFCC-side build scope. A first draft has been produced by Jhoan Rose Dela Cruz and shared on Confluence using the TSD template provided by the team. This ticket covers the structured review, feedback incorporation, and sign-off of that document before it is published as a finalised deliverable.\nTasks\nReview the TSD draft on Confluence against the integration pattern and data flow documented in SFCC-123\nValidate that the content model structure, locale configuration, and SFCC-side build scope are accurately captured\nConfirm the handoff boundary between what Accenture builds and what the incoming Contentful squad owns is clearly defined\nProvide consolidated written feedback on the Confluence draft\nIncorporate review feedback and update the document accordingly\nObtain sign-off from the BA Lead and Solution Architect before closing\nDefinition of Done\nThe Contentful Integration TSD is reviewed, feedback is incorporated, and the document is signed off by the BA Lead and Solution Architect — published on Confluence and ready to be shared with the incoming Contentful squad as a finalised briefing artefact.",
