      "key": "SFCC-257",
      "summary": "Spike: Playwright Spec Generation from Zephyr Test Cases",
      "description": "Objective\nInvestigate and document how a Dev/Tester generates Playwright spec files from Zephyr test cases — so the squad has a confirmed, repeatable pattern for converting documented test cases into executable automation scripts.\nBackground\nZephyr test cases define what to test; Playwright specs define how to automate it. The gap between the two is currently manual and inconsistent. This spike confirms the workflow: who generates the spec, what inputs they use from Zephyr, how the spec is structured, and where it lives in the repository.\nTasks\nConfirm the source format: what fields from a Zephyr test case map to a Playwright spec (test name, steps, assertions, data)\nDefine who is responsible for spec generation — Dev, Tester, or shared — and when in the sprint cycle this happens\nDocument the spec file structure and naming convention to be used across the project\nConfirm where Playwright specs are stored in the repository and how they are linked back to Zephyr test cases\nIdentify any tooling or templates that accelerate spec generation from Zephyr\nDefinition of Done\nA documented pattern confirming how Playwright specs are generated from Zephyr test cases, including ownership, file structure, naming convention, repository location, and a worked example — with Technical Lead sign-off and sufficient detail for any Dev or Tester on the squad to follow.",
